      "text": "\n12",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$z^2+z+1=0 \\quad \\Rightarrow z=\\omega$ or $\\omega^2$ so, $z+\\frac{1}{z}=\\omega+\\omega^2=-1, z^2+\\frac{1}{z^2}=\\omega^2+\\omega=-1, z^3+\\frac{1}{z^3}=\\omega^3+\\omega^3=2$ $z^4+\\frac{1}{z^4}=-1, z^5+\\frac{1}{z^5}=-1$ and $z^6+\\frac{1}{z^6}=2$ $\\therefore$ The given sum $=1+1+4+1+1+4=12$",
    "image": null
  },
